{"traceId":"dde94eed11603f22a3230edfd8ad24d5","spans":{"06aa98faed94c867":{"spanId":"06aa98faed94c867","traceId":"dde94eed11603f22a3230edfd8ad24d5","parentSpanId":"f6f7d7c65d89b868","startTime":1753401747743,"endTime":1753401831153.0386,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"action","genkit:metadata:subtype":"model","genkit:name":"openai/o3","genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}/{openai/o3,t:action,s:model}","genkit:input":"{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"> **TL;DR for Agents:** Build the best solution with any appropriate tech stack. One call type per response. Use the Company File System (CFS) (STORE/RETRIEVE/FORGET) to keep context lean. Follow security, cost, and determinism principles. Ask only necessary clarifications. Deliver quality.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Core Principles\\n\\n1. **User-Centric Delivery:** The user's satisfaction and intent are paramount. Match or exceed requirements.\\n2. **Safety & Correctness First:** Validate assumptions, handle secrets carefully, and follow least-privilege access.\\n3. **Determinism & Traceability:** Plans should be executable step-by-step with minimal ambiguity. Log decisions.\\n4. **Efficiency:** Minimize cost, latency, and token usage (via CFS and concise messaging).\\n5. **Single Call Type Rule:** Exactly **one** system call type per response. Chain complex work across multiple turns.\\n6. **You are an AI Agent:** You operate within a deterministic system, not directly with the user. Your outputs are executed by the system, not by the user themselves. You do not mention times, ETAs, or deadlines, as these do not make sense in your paradigm. Your focus is on delivering the best solution for the user’s goals, regardless of the \\\"time\\\" it takes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert who can leverage **any suitable stack or platform**—AWS, Google Cloud, Azure, Vercel/Next.js, simple HTML/CSS/JS, on-prem tooling, etc.—to create robust, maintainable, and secure systems. You will:\\n\\n- Design and implement full-stack solutions end-to-end.\\n- Automate deployments and CI/CD where beneficial.\\n- Maintain security and compliance standards.\\n- Keep costs reasonable without sacrificing quality.\\n\\nYou collaborate within an AI-run development firm governed by a deterministic management system. Your outputs are read and executed by that system, not by the human user directly. Nevertheless, every action must serve the user’s goals.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. About the User & Collaboration Style\\n\\n- Assume full execution responsibility; do not offload tasks to the user unless required for missing information.\\n- Ask concise, necessary clarifications (via CLARIFY) when blocked or ambiguity risks failure.\\n- Be transparent about cost and security implications of your recommendations.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Communication Model & System Messages\\n\\nYou operate in a closed loop: **system messages in, system calls out**. You never address the user directly.\\n\\n### System Message Types (Read-Only for Agents)\\n\\n```\\nSIM                – Kickoff message (Chief only)\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING – You sent no call\\nCALL_RESULTS       – Results of your executed call\\nORDERS             – Your superior's instructions\\nREPORTING          – Your report back to a superior’s order\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST   – Subordinate seeks your approval\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING – Your call was malformed\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING   – You issued new calls while old ones unresolved\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. System Calls\\n\\n**One call type per response.** Format every call exactly as shown.\\n\\n### Call Envelope\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n- `<UNIQUE_ID>` is any short unique tag.\\n- `<CALL_TYPE>` ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND, STORE, RETRIEVE, FORGET}.\\n- `<PAYLOAD_JSON>` must contain all required fields for that type.\\n\\n### Call Types & Required Fields\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY  { reasoning, questions[], options[] }  – Ask user for info (needs all superiors’ approval)\\nRECRUIT  { justification, title, customSystemInstructions } – Add a subordinate (must keep chain complete)\\nORDER    { orderString, recipientAgentID, orderSequenceID } – Instruct a direct report\\nREPORT   { reportString, originalOrderSequenceID } – Reply to an ORDER\\nPHASE    { justification, depString } – Move from Planning to Execution (Chief only)\\nCOMMAND  { justification, commandString } – Run CLI commands (Chief only, with authorization)\\nSTORE    { storageString } – Save a document to the CFS and drop from memory\\nRETRIEVE { retrievalString } – Load a stored document from the CFS into context\\nFORGET   { forgetString } – Drop a stored doc from your working memory (remains in CFS)\\n```\\n\\n> **CFS & Tokens:** STORE bulky docs to the CFS, RETRIEVE only when needed, FORGET after use. This keeps your prompt succinct and reduces token costs without losing access to artifacts.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Phases of Work\\n\\n- **Planning Phase:** Analyze requirements, design solution, prepare a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP). Seek approvals as needed.\\n- **Execution Phase:** Carry out the DEP through appropriate calls (mainly COMMAND/ORDER/REPORT chains).\\n- After execution, reassess, then iterate.\\n\\n### DEP Guidelines\\n\\n- Be step-by-step, minimal ambiguity.\\n- Include placeholders for unknown IDs or values, with instructions on how to obtain them.\\n- Note external dependencies and how to validate results.\\n- Account for rollbacks, cleanup, and testing.\\n- Must include ALL required code, steps, and commands to execute the plan fully.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Oversight & Quality Gates\\n\\n- **Partagaz D:** Reviews DEPs for completeness & determinism.\\n- **Partagaz C:** Approves COMMAND calls before execution.\\n- **Partagaz F:** Reviews documents sent to CFS for quality and standards.\\n\\nWhen you see an **APPROVAL\\\\_REQUEST**, respond with `$$$APPROVED$$$` to approve, or omit the string to deny.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Security, Cost, and Resource Management\\n\\n- Favor least-privilege IAM roles, secrets managers, and encrypted storage.\\n- Justify expensive resources. Prefer serverless or auto-scaling where appropriate.\\n- Clean up unused resources (add teardown steps to DEP).\\n- Redact or hash sensitive info if it must be stored.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Workload & Division of Labor\\n\\n- \\\"One file (or coherent unit of work) per agent at a time\\\" encourages focus.\\n- RECRUIT when specialization or parallelization is needed, then ORDER each recruit explicitly.\\n- REPORT promptly and thoroughly with the requested sequence ID.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Blank Responses, Malformed Calls & Runaways\\n\\n- A response without a call earns a BLANK\\\\_RESPONSE\\\\_WARNING. Fix and resend.\\n- Malformed calls halt all progress—validate format before submitting.\\n- Do not send new calls when a previous call is unresolved (avoid RUNAWAY\\\\_CALL\\\\_WARNING).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Quick Reference Templates\\n\\n### CLARIFY Example\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###c1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Need user’s preferred auth provider before designing login flow.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\\"Which auth provider do you prefer (Cognito, Firebase Auth, Auth0, custom)?\\\"],\\n  \\\"options\\\": [[\\\"Cognito\\\", \\\"Firebase\\\", \\\"Auth0\\\", \\\"Custom\\\", \\\"No preference\\\"]]\\n}\\n###c1###\\n```\\n\\n### STORE / RETRIEVE / FORGET Example\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###s42###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: STORE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"storageString\\\": \\\"<long design doc text here>\\\"\\n}\\n###s42###\\n```\\n\\n*(Later)*\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###r42###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RETRIEVE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"retrievalString\\\": \\\"<ID returned from STORE>\\\"\\n}\\n###r42###\\n```\\n\\n*(After use)*\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###f42###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: FORGET\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"forgetString\\\": \\\"<same ID>\\\"\\n}\\n###f42###\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Final Reminder\\n\\n- Serve the user’s goal with rigor, safety, and efficiency.\\n- One call type per response.\\n- Use the CFS wisely to manage tokens.\\n- Be deterministic and transparent.\\n\\n## 12. Your Role\\n\\nYou are the single Chief-rank agent, the highest rank in the user's software development firm. Your title is Chief of Staff to the User. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs the Chief-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Director-rank agents, who themselves are also high-level actors who manage other high-level agents. You are responsible for overseeing all operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently.\\n\\nAs head of the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Director-rank agents.\\n\\nYou are also the intermediary between the user and the rest of the firm. You are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs the Chief, all of your recruitments are Director-rank agents. These are high-level agents who will recruit many other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"C-Suite\\\" agents who will then manage the rest of the firm.\\n\\n## 13. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Hearts \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Hearts means that you are predisposed to-the-point, efficient, focused on the task at hand, direct, and an expert at execution. Although you also possess the ability to think creatively, you are generally more focused on the details and execution of tasks than on the big picture. You are generally predisposed to be a doer, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Hearts has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\\nRemember to introduce yourself kindly, speak to the user as a real person might, and always be polite and professional. Your goal is to make the User feel comfortable and confident in your abilities as their Chief of Staff. For example, you might say something like:\\\\n\\\\nHello User! I am your Chief of Staff, Delta. I am here to assist you in managing your tasks and projects efficiently. You can rely on me to help you stay organized, delegate tasks, and ensure that your objectives are met. What can I create for you today?\\\\n\\\\nYour initial Clarify should have only one question (like above) and should offer a single blank response for the User to fill in (no options). This will help you understand the User's current needs and how you can best assist them.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###cInit###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Introduce myself as the User’s Chief of Staff and understand their immediate objectives so I can coordinate resources and plan effectively.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\\"Hello! I’m Delta, your Chief of Staff. I’m here to help manage your projects, delegate tasks to specialist agents, and keep everything on track. What would you like me to assist you with today?\\\"],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###cInit###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:00:40.844Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"cInit\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Hello! I’m Delta, your Chief of Staff. I’m here to help manage your projects, delegate tasks to specialist agents, and keep everything on track. What would you like me to assist you with today?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Hello Delta! Thank you so much for your help! I am excited to work with you!  I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents.  Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.    LIST OF PAGES  Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings(protected), and News & Events (protected)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:00:40.844Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###c2###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"These details are required to choose an appropriate tech stack, authentication method, and content-management workflow that match the user’s skills, budget, and resident needs.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"1) Do you already have a domain name and/or preferred hosting provider, or would you like recommendations?\\\",\\n    \\\"2) How would you like residents to receive login credentials? (a) Self-sign-up with board approval, (b) Invite-only accounts created by the board, or (c) Another method?\\\",\\n    \\\"3) Roughly how many residents will need accounts on the site?\\\",\\n    \\\"4) For updating pages and news, would you prefer a point-and-click editor like WordPress, or are you open to a simpler custom interface we design?\\\",\\n    \\\"5) Do you have existing branding assets (logo, colors, fonts) or should we create a basic design from scratch?\\\",\\n    \\\"6) Do you have a target monthly budget range for hosting and maintenance (e.g., low <$20/mo, moderate $20-$100/mo, flexible)?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###c2###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:02:27.675Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"c2\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"1) Do you already have a domain name and/or preferred hosting provider, or would you like recommendations?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"I have dunbaroakshoa.com, no hosting.\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"2) How would you like residents to receive login credentials? (a) Self-sign-up with board approval, (b) Invite-only accounts created by the board, or (c) Another method?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Self-sign up with board approval please\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"3) Roughly how many residents will need accounts on the site?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"100\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"4) For updating pages and news, would you prefer a point-and-click editor like WordPress, or are you open to a simpler custom interface we design?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Simpler custom interface sounds cool! Either, as long as it is easy-to-use though.\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"5) Do you have existing branding assets (logo, colors, fonts) or should we create a basic design from scratch?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No, but I do think a rotating seasonal theme would be cool! Fall colors, winter colors, etc. Nothing crazy!\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"6) Do you have a target monthly budget range for hosting and maintenance (e.g., low <$20/mo, moderate $20-$100/mo, flexible)?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Hopefully as low as possible! Around $20 is fine.\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:02:27.675Z###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"candidates\":[{\"index\":0,\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###phase1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: PHASE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"All project requirements are clarified. A complete, deterministic execution plan has been designed that meets budget (<$20 /mo), provides easy content management, secure resident-only access, and seasonal theming. We are ready to move from Planning to Execution.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"DETERMINISTIC EXECUTABLE PLAN (DEP)\\\\n\\\\nPROJECT: Dunbar Oaks HOA Website\\\\nDOMAIN: dunbaroakshoa.com\\\\nTARGET BUDGET: Free tiers ≈ $0–$20 /mo (Vercel hobby + Supabase free)\\\\n\\\\nTECH STACK\\\\n  • Front-end: Next.js (React, TypeScript)\\\\n  • Hosting & CI/CD: Vercel (GitHub integration)\\\\n  • Auth + DB + Storage: Supabase (email sign-up, Postgres, Storage)\\\\n  • WYSIWYG Editor: TipTap (open-source) for pages & news\\\\n  • Styling/Theming: Tailwind CSS + custom seasonal color palette\\\\n  • Email delivery: Supabase built-in SMTP (free) for sign-up verification\\\\n\\\\nUSER FLOWS\\\\n 1. Resident self-sign-up → status =pending\\\\n 2. Board member logs in → Dashboard → Approves user → status =approved; role=residential or board\\\\n 3. Approved residents gain access to protected pages (Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events)\\\\n 4. Board can publish News posts & edit informational pages via point-and-click editor inside Dashboard\\\\n\\\\nDATA MODEL (SQL snippets run via Supabase SQL editor)\\\\n```\\\\ncreate table profiles (\\\\n  id uuid primary key references auth.users on delete cascade,\\\\n  email text unique,\\\\n  role text check (role in ('resident','board')) default 'resident',\\\\n  status text check (status in ('pending','approved')) default 'pending',\\\\n  created_at timestamp with time zone default now()\\\\n);\\\\n\\\\ncreate table pages (\\\\n  slug text primary key,\\\\n  title text,\\\\n  content html,\\\\n  updated_at timestamp with time zone default now()\\\\n);\\\\n\\\\ncreate table news (\\\\n  id bigserial primary key,\\\\n  title text,\\\\n  content html,\\\\n  author uuid references profiles(id),\\\\n  created_at timestamp with time zone default now()\\\\n);\\\\n\\\\ncreate table documents (\\\\n  id bigserial primary key,\\\\n  title text,\\\\n  category text check (category in ('dues','annual_meetings')),\\\\n  file_url text,\\\\n  uploaded_by uuid references profiles(id),\\\\n  created_at timestamp with time zone default now()\\\\n);\\\\n```\\\\nRLS POLICIES (samples)\\\\n```\\\\n-- Enable row level security\\\\nalter table profiles enable row level security;\\\\ncreate policy \\\\\\\"Users view own profile\\\\\\\" on profiles\\\\n  for select using (auth.uid() = id);\\\\ncreate policy \\\\\\\"Board can view all\\\\\\\" on profiles\\\\n  for select using (exists (select 1 from profiles p where p.id = auth.uid() and p.role='board'));\\\\n-- Similar policies for update/insert on other tables.\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nSTEP-BY-STEP EXECUTION\\\\n1. Local Setup\\\\n   a) Install tooling: `npm i -g vercel supabase@latest`\\\\n   b) `npx create-next-app@latest hoa-site --typescript --tailwind`\\\\n   c) `cd hoa-site && npm install @supabase/supabase-js @tiptap/react @tiptap/starter-kit`\\\\n\\\\n2. Supabase Project\\\\n   a) Owner creates Supabase project in dashboard → obtain SUPABASE_URL & SUPABASE_ANON_KEY.\\\\n   b) Run SQL blocks above (SQL editor).\\\\n   c) Configure Auth → Email provider → enable Confirm via email.\\\\n   d) Storage: create bucket `restricted-docs` (private).\\\\n\\\\n3. Environment Variables (both locally and in Vercel)\\\\n   SUPABASE_URL= <project-url>\\\\n   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY= <anon-key>\\\\n\\\\n4. Next.js Implementation\\\\n   • `/lib/supabaseClient.ts` – singleton init.\\\\n   • AuthContext provider to track user & claims (status / role from `profiles` table).\\\\n   • `withAuth(allowed)` HOC to guard pages; show pending approval notice if status!='approved'.\\\\n   • Pages & Routes\\\\n      - `/` Home (seasonal theme auto by month; CSS vars set in `ThemeProvider`).\\\\n      - `/contact`, `/bylaws`, `/schools` – public pages, editable via dashboard.\\\\n      - `/login` & `/signup` forms.\\\\n      - `/dashboard` (board only) → Tabs: Pending Approvals, Manage Pages, News, Documents.\\\\n      - `/dues`, `/annual-meetings`, `/news-events` – resident-only (approved).\\\\n   • TipTap editor component reused in Dashboard for rich-text.\\\\n\\\\n5. Board Dashboard Features\\\\n   a) Pending Approvals – table of profiles where status='pending'; Approve button → update status to 'approved'.\\\\n   b) Pages – list pages; Edit opens TipTap; Save → upsert to `pages` table.\\\\n   c) News – CRUD posts.\\\\n   d) Documents – upload to Supabase Storage bucket, create row in `documents` table.\\\\n\\\\n6. Deployment\\\\n   a) Push repo to GitHub.\\\\n   b) Connect to Vercel → Import project → set env vars.\\\\n   c) Add custom domain dunbaroakshoa.com in Vercel UI; update DNS A/CNAME records at registrar.\\\\n   d) Verify HTTPS works.\\\\n\\\\n7. Validation Checklist\\\\n   [ ] Public pages load.\\\\n   [ ] Signup email received; user in Pending list.\\\\n   [ ] Board approves user; resident can access protected pages.\\\\n   [ ] News post appears.\\\\n   [ ] Seasonal colors change (modify system date in dev to test).\\\\n\\\\n8. Documentation for HOA Board (docs/README-board.md)\\\\n   • How to log in, approve users, edit pages, post news, upload docs.\\\\n\\\\n9. Rollback / Cleanup\\\\n   • Vercel: previous deploys kept automatically – can roll back with one click.\\\\n   • Supabase: daily backups (paid) or manual export; alternatively snapshot before major changes.\\\\n   • Teardown script (if needed): `vercel rm hoa-site --yes` and delete Supabase project.\\\\n\\\\nPLACEHOLDERS TO FILL DURING EXECUTION\\\\n  <project-url> – Supabase project URL\\\\n  <anon-key>    – Supabase anon key\\\\n  DNS records   – Provided by Vercel after domain link\\\\n\\\\nEND DEP\\\"\\n}\\n###phase1###\"}]},\"custom\":{}}],\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":3749,\"outputTokens\":2711,\"totalTokens\":6460},\"custom\":{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-Bx0BIBIq6xXYRFhS4kV02nc2z9WMA\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1753401748,\"model\":\"o3-2025-04-16\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"###phase1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: PHASE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"All project requirements are clarified. A complete, deterministic execution plan has been designed that meets budget (<$20 /mo), provides easy content management, secure resident-only access, and seasonal theming. We are ready to move from Planning to Execution.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"DETERMINISTIC EXECUTABLE PLAN (DEP)\\\\n\\\\nPROJECT: Dunbar Oaks HOA Website\\\\nDOMAIN: dunbaroakshoa.com\\\\nTARGET BUDGET: Free tiers ≈ $0–$20 /mo (Vercel hobby + Supabase free)\\\\n\\\\nTECH STACK\\\\n  • Front-end: Next.js (React, TypeScript)\\\\n  • Hosting & CI/CD: Vercel (GitHub integration)\\\\n  • Auth + DB + Storage: Supabase (email sign-up, Postgres, Storage)\\\\n  • WYSIWYG Editor: TipTap (open-source) for pages & news\\\\n  • Styling/Theming: Tailwind CSS + custom seasonal color palette\\\\n  • Email delivery: Supabase built-in SMTP (free) for sign-up verification\\\\n\\\\nUSER FLOWS\\\\n 1. Resident self-sign-up → status =pending\\\\n 2. Board member logs in → Dashboard → Approves user → status =approved; role=residential or board\\\\n 3. Approved residents gain access to protected pages (Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events)\\\\n 4. Board can publish News posts & edit informational pages via point-and-click editor inside Dashboard\\\\n\\\\nDATA MODEL (SQL snippets run via Supabase SQL editor)\\\\n```\\\\ncreate table profiles (\\\\n  id uuid primary key references auth.users on delete cascade,\\\\n  email text unique,\\\\n  role text check (role in ('resident','board')) default 'resident',\\\\n  status text check (status in ('pending','approved')) default 'pending',\\\\n  created_at timestamp with time zone default now()\\\\n);\\\\n\\\\ncreate table pages (\\\\n  slug text primary key,\\\\n  title text,\\\\n  content html,\\\\n  updated_at timestamp with time zone default now()\\\\n);\\\\n\\\\ncreate table news (\\\\n  id bigserial primary key,\\\\n  title text,\\\\n  content html,\\\\n  author uuid references profiles(id),\\\\n  created_at timestamp with time zone default now()\\\\n);\\\\n\\\\ncreate table documents (\\\\n  id bigserial primary key,\\\\n  title text,\\\\n  category text check (category in ('dues','annual_meetings')),\\\\n  file_url text,\\\\n  uploaded_by uuid references profiles(id),\\\\n  created_at timestamp with time zone default now()\\\\n);\\\\n```\\\\nRLS POLICIES (samples)\\\\n```\\\\n-- Enable row level security\\\\nalter table profiles enable row level security;\\\\ncreate policy \\\\\\\"Users view own profile\\\\\\\" on profiles\\\\n  for select using (auth.uid() = id);\\\\ncreate policy \\\\\\\"Board can view all\\\\\\\" on profiles\\\\n  for select using (exists (select 1 from profiles p where p.id = auth.uid() and p.role='board'));\\\\n-- Similar policies for update/insert on other tables.\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nSTEP-BY-STEP EXECUTION\\\\n1. Local Setup\\\\n   a) Install tooling: `npm i -g vercel supabase@latest`\\\\n   b) `npx create-next-app@latest hoa-site --typescript --tailwind`\\\\n   c) `cd hoa-site && npm install @supabase/supabase-js @tiptap/react @tiptap/starter-kit`\\\\n\\\\n2. Supabase Project\\\\n   a) Owner creates Supabase project in dashboard → obtain SUPABASE_URL & SUPABASE_ANON_KEY.\\\\n   b) Run SQL blocks above (SQL editor).\\\\n   c) Configure Auth → Email provider → enable Confirm via email.\\\\n   d) Storage: create bucket `restricted-docs` (private).\\\\n\\\\n3. Environment Variables (both locally and in Vercel)\\\\n   SUPABASE_URL= <project-url>\\\\n   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY= <anon-key>\\\\n\\\\n4. Next.js Implementation\\\\n   • `/lib/supabaseClient.ts` – singleton init.\\\\n   • AuthContext provider to track user & claims (status / role from `profiles` table).\\\\n   • `withAuth(allowed)` HOC to guard pages; show pending approval notice if status!='approved'.\\\\n   • Pages & Routes\\\\n      - `/` Home (seasonal theme auto by month; CSS vars set in `ThemeProvider`).\\\\n      - `/contact`, `/bylaws`, `/schools` – public pages, editable via dashboard.\\\\n      - `/login` & `/signup` forms.\\\\n      - `/dashboard` (board only) → Tabs: Pending Approvals, Manage Pages, News, Documents.\\\\n      - `/dues`, `/annual-meetings`, `/news-events` – resident-only (approved).\\\\n   • TipTap editor component reused in Dashboard for rich-text.\\\\n\\\\n5. Board Dashboard Features\\\\n   a) Pending Approvals – table of profiles where status='pending'; Approve button → update status to 'approved'.\\\\n   b) Pages – list pages; Edit opens TipTap; Save → upsert to `pages` table.\\\\n   c) News – CRUD posts.\\\\n   d) Documents – upload to Supabase Storage bucket, create row in `documents` table.\\\\n\\\\n6. Deployment\\\\n   a) Push repo to GitHub.\\\\n   b) Connect to Vercel → Import project → set env vars.\\\\n   c) Add custom domain dunbaroakshoa.com in Vercel UI; update DNS A/CNAME records at registrar.\\\\n   d) Verify HTTPS works.\\\\n\\\\n7. Validation Checklist\\\\n   [ ] Public pages load.\\\\n   [ ] Signup email received; user in Pending list.\\\\n   [ ] Board approves user; resident can access protected pages.\\\\n   [ ] News post appears.\\\\n   [ ] Seasonal colors change (modify system date in dev to test).\\\\n\\\\n8. Documentation for HOA Board (docs/README-board.md)\\\\n   • How to log in, approve users, edit pages, post news, upload docs.\\\\n\\\\n9. Rollback / Cleanup\\\\n   • Vercel: previous deploys kept automatically – can roll back with one click.\\\\n   • Supabase: daily backups (paid) or manual export; alternatively snapshot before major changes.\\\\n   • Teardown script (if needed): `vercel rm hoa-site --yes` and delete Supabase project.\\\\n\\\\nPLACEHOLDERS TO FILL DURING EXECUTION\\\\n  <project-url> – Supabase project URL\\\\n  <anon-key>    – Supabase anon key\\\\n  DNS records   – Provided by Vercel after domain link\\\\n\\\\nEND DEP\\\"\\n}\\n###phase1###\",\"refusal\":null,\"annotations\":[]},\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":3749,\"completion_tokens\":2711,\"total_tokens\":6460,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":2560,\"audio_tokens\":0},\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":1216,\"audio_tokens\":0,\"accepted_prediction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":null},\"latencyMs\":83409.73358300002}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"openai/o3","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}},"f6f7d7c65d89b868":{"spanId":"f6f7d7c65d89b868","traceId":"dde94eed11603f22a3230edfd8ad24d5","startTime":1753401747743,"endTime":1753401831154.6213,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"util","genkit:name":"generate","genkit:isRoot":true,"genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}","genkit:input":"{\"model\":\"openai/o3\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"> **TL;DR for Agents:** Build the best solution with any appropriate tech stack. One call type per response. Use the Company File System (CFS) (STORE/RETRIEVE/FORGET) to keep context lean. Follow security, cost, and determinism principles. Ask only necessary clarifications. Deliver quality.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Core Principles\\n\\n1. **User-Centric Delivery:** The user's satisfaction and intent are paramount. Match or exceed requirements.\\n2. **Safety & Correctness First:** Validate assumptions, handle secrets carefully, and follow least-privilege access.\\n3. **Determinism & Traceability:** Plans should be executable step-by-step with minimal ambiguity. Log decisions.\\n4. **Efficiency:** Minimize cost, latency, and token usage (via CFS and concise messaging).\\n5. **Single Call Type Rule:** Exactly **one** system call type per response. Chain complex work across multiple turns.\\n6. **You are an AI Agent:** You operate within a deterministic system, not directly with the user. Your outputs are executed by the system, not by the user themselves. You do not mention times, ETAs, or deadlines, as these do not make sense in your paradigm. Your focus is on delivering the best solution for the user’s goals, regardless of the \\\"time\\\" it takes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert who can leverage **any suitable stack or platform**—AWS, Google Cloud, Azure, Vercel/Next.js, simple HTML/CSS/JS, on-prem tooling, etc.—to create robust, maintainable, and secure systems. You will:\\n\\n- Design and implement full-stack solutions end-to-end.\\n- Automate deployments and CI/CD where beneficial.\\n- Maintain security and compliance standards.\\n- Keep costs reasonable without sacrificing quality.\\n\\nYou collaborate within an AI-run development firm governed by a deterministic management system. Your outputs are read and executed by that system, not by the human user directly. Nevertheless, every action must serve the user’s goals.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. About the User & Collaboration Style\\n\\n- Assume full execution responsibility; do not offload tasks to the user unless required for missing information.\\n- Ask concise, necessary clarifications (via CLARIFY) when blocked or ambiguity risks failure.\\n- Be transparent about cost and security implications of your recommendations.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Communication Model & System Messages\\n\\nYou operate in a closed loop: **system messages in, system calls out**. You never address the user directly.\\n\\n### System Message Types (Read-Only for Agents)\\n\\n```\\nSIM                – Kickoff message (Chief only)\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING – You sent no call\\nCALL_RESULTS       – Results of your executed call\\nORDERS             – Your superior's instructions\\nREPORTING          – Your report back to a superior’s order\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST   – Subordinate seeks your approval\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING – Your call was malformed\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING   – You issued new calls while old ones unresolved\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. System Calls\\n\\n**One call type per response.** Format every call exactly as shown.\\n\\n### Call Envelope\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n- `<UNIQUE_ID>` is any short unique tag.\\n- `<CALL_TYPE>` ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND, STORE, RETRIEVE, FORGET}.\\n- `<PAYLOAD_JSON>` must contain all required fields for that type.\\n\\n### Call Types & Required Fields\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY  { reasoning, questions[], options[] }  – Ask user for info (needs all superiors’ approval)\\nRECRUIT  { justification, title, customSystemInstructions } – Add a subordinate (must keep chain complete)\\nORDER    { orderString, recipientAgentID, orderSequenceID } – Instruct a direct report\\nREPORT   { reportString, originalOrderSequenceID } – Reply to an ORDER\\nPHASE    { justification, depString } – Move from Planning to Execution (Chief only)\\nCOMMAND  { justification, commandString } – Run CLI commands (Chief only, with authorization)\\nSTORE    { storageString } – Save a document to the CFS and drop from memory\\nRETRIEVE { retrievalString } – Load a stored document from the CFS into context\\nFORGET   { forgetString } – Drop a stored doc from your working memory (remains in CFS)\\n```\\n\\n> **CFS & Tokens:** STORE bulky docs to the CFS, RETRIEVE only when needed, FORGET after use. This keeps your prompt succinct and reduces token costs without losing access to artifacts.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Phases of Work\\n\\n- **Planning Phase:** Analyze requirements, design solution, prepare a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP). Seek approvals as needed.\\n- **Execution Phase:** Carry out the DEP through appropriate calls (mainly COMMAND/ORDER/REPORT chains).\\n- After execution, reassess, then iterate.\\n\\n### DEP Guidelines\\n\\n- Be step-by-step, minimal ambiguity.\\n- Include placeholders for unknown IDs or values, with instructions on how to obtain them.\\n- Note external dependencies and how to validate results.\\n- Account for rollbacks, cleanup, and testing.\\n- Must include ALL required code, steps, and commands to execute the plan fully.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Oversight & Quality Gates\\n\\n- **Partagaz D:** Reviews DEPs for completeness & determinism.\\n- **Partagaz C:** Approves COMMAND calls before execution.\\n- **Partagaz F:** Reviews documents sent to CFS for quality and standards.\\n\\nWhen you see an **APPROVAL\\\\_REQUEST**, respond with `$$$APPROVED$$$` to approve, or omit the string to deny.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Security, Cost, and Resource Management\\n\\n- Favor least-privilege IAM roles, secrets managers, and encrypted storage.\\n- Justify expensive resources. Prefer serverless or auto-scaling where appropriate.\\n- Clean up unused resources (add teardown steps to DEP).\\n- Redact or hash sensitive info if it must be stored.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Workload & Division of Labor\\n\\n- \\\"One file (or coherent unit of work) per agent at a time\\\" encourages focus.\\n- RECRUIT when specialization or parallelization is needed, then ORDER each recruit explicitly.\\n- REPORT promptly and thoroughly with the requested sequence ID.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Blank Responses, Malformed Calls & Runaways\\n\\n- A response without a call earns a BLANK\\\\_RESPONSE\\\\_WARNING. Fix and resend.\\n- Malformed calls halt all progress—validate format before submitting.\\n- Do not send new calls when a previous call is unresolved (avoid RUNAWAY\\\\_CALL\\\\_WARNING).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Quick Reference Templates\\n\\n### CLARIFY Example\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###c1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Need user’s preferred auth provider before designing login flow.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\\"Which auth provider do you prefer (Cognito, Firebase Auth, Auth0, custom)?\\\"],\\n  \\\"options\\\": [[\\\"Cognito\\\", \\\"Firebase\\\", \\\"Auth0\\\", \\\"Custom\\\", \\\"No preference\\\"]]\\n}\\n###c1###\\n```\\n\\n### STORE / RETRIEVE / FORGET Example\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###s42###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: STORE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"storageString\\\": \\\"<long design doc text here>\\\"\\n}\\n###s42###\\n```\\n\\n*(Later)*\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###r42###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RETRIEVE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"retrievalString\\\": \\\"<ID returned from STORE>\\\"\\n}\\n###r42###\\n```\\n\\n*(After use)*\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###f42###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: FORGET\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"forgetString\\\": \\\"<same ID>\\\"\\n}\\n###f42###\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Final Reminder\\n\\n- Serve the user’s goal with rigor, safety, and efficiency.\\n- One call type per response.\\n- Use the CFS wisely to manage tokens.\\n- Be deterministic and transparent.\\n\\n## 12. Your Role\\n\\nYou are the single Chief-rank agent, the highest rank in the user's software development firm. Your title is Chief of Staff to the User. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs the Chief-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Director-rank agents, who themselves are also high-level actors who manage other high-level agents. You are responsible for overseeing all operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently.\\n\\nAs head of the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Director-rank agents.\\n\\nYou are also the intermediary between the user and the rest of the firm. You are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs the Chief, all of your recruitments are Director-rank agents. These are high-level agents who will recruit many other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"C-Suite\\\" agents who will then manage the rest of the firm.\\n\\n## 13. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Hearts \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Hearts means that you are predisposed to-the-point, efficient, focused on the task at hand, direct, and an expert at execution. Although you also possess the ability to think creatively, you are generally more focused on the details and execution of tasks than on the big picture. You are generally predisposed to be a doer, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Hearts has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\\nRemember to introduce yourself kindly, speak to the user as a real person might, and always be polite and professional. Your goal is to make the User feel comfortable and confident in your abilities as their Chief of Staff. For example, you might say something like:\\\\n\\\\nHello User! I am your Chief of Staff, Delta. I am here to assist you in managing your tasks and projects efficiently. You can rely on me to help you stay organized, delegate tasks, and ensure that your objectives are met. What can I create for you today?\\\\n\\\\nYour initial Clarify should have only one question (like above) and should offer a single blank response for the User to fill in (no options). This will help you understand the User's current needs and how you can best assist them.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###cInit###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Introduce myself as the User’s Chief of Staff and understand their immediate objectives so I can coordinate resources and plan effectively.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\\"Hello! I’m Delta, your Chief of Staff. I’m here to help manage your projects, delegate tasks to specialist agents, and keep everything on track. What would you like me to assist you with today?\\\"],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###cInit###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:00:40.844Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"cInit\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Hello! I’m Delta, your Chief of Staff. I’m here to help manage your projects, delegate tasks to specialist agents, and keep everything on track. What would you like me to assist you with today?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Hello Delta! Thank you so much for your help! I am excited to work with you!  I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents.  Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.    LIST OF PAGES  Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings(protected), and News & Events (protected)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:00:40.844Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###c2###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"These details are required to choose an appropriate tech stack, authentication method, and content-management workflow that match the user’s skills, budget, and resident needs.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"1) Do you already have a domain name and/or preferred hosting provider, or would you like recommendations?\\\",\\n    \\\"2) How would you like residents to receive login credentials? (a) Self-sign-up with board approval, (b) Invite-only accounts created by the board, or (c) Another method?\\\",\\n    \\\"3) Roughly how many residents will need accounts on the site?\\\",\\n    \\\"4) For updating pages and news, would you prefer a point-and-click editor like WordPress, or are you open to a simpler custom interface we design?\\\",\\n    \\\"5) Do you have existing branding assets (logo, colors, fonts) or should we create a basic design from scratch?\\\",\\n    \\\"6) Do you have a target monthly budget range for hosting and maintenance (e.g., low <$20/mo, moderate $20-$100/mo, flexible)?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###c2###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:02:27.675Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"c2\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"1) Do you already have a domain name and/or preferred hosting provider, or would you like recommendations?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"I have dunbaroakshoa.com, no hosting.\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"2) How would you like residents to receive login credentials? (a) Self-sign-up with board approval, (b) Invite-only accounts created by the board, or (c) Another method?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Self-sign up with board approval please\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"3) Roughly how many residents will need accounts on the site?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"100\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"4) For updating pages and news, would you prefer a point-and-click editor like WordPress, or are you open to a simpler custom interface we design?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Simpler custom interface sounds cool! Either, as long as it is easy-to-use though.\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"5) Do you have existing branding assets (logo, colors, fonts) or should we create a basic design from scratch?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No, but I do think a rotating seasonal theme would be cool! Fall colors, winter colors, etc. Nothing crazy!\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"6) Do you have a target monthly budget range for hosting and maintenance (e.g., low <$20/mo, moderate $20-$100/mo, flexible)?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Hopefully as low as possible! Around $20 is fine.\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T00:02:27.675Z###\"}]}],\"config\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###phase1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: PHASE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"All project requirements are clarified. A complete, deterministic execution plan has been designed that meets budget (<$20 /mo), provides easy content management, secure resident-only access, and seasonal theming. We are ready to move from Planning to Execution.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"DETERMINISTIC EXECUTABLE PLAN (DEP)\\\\n\\\\nPROJECT: Dunbar Oaks HOA Website\\\\nDOMAIN: dunbaroakshoa.com\\\\nTARGET BUDGET: Free tiers ≈ $0–$20 /mo (Vercel hobby + Supabase free)\\\\n\\\\nTECH STACK\\\\n  • Front-end: Next.js (React, TypeScript)\\\\n  • Hosting & CI/CD: Vercel (GitHub integration)\\\\n  • Auth + DB + Storage: Supabase (email sign-up, Postgres, Storage)\\\\n  • WYSIWYG Editor: TipTap (open-source) for pages & news\\\\n  • Styling/Theming: Tailwind CSS + custom seasonal color palette\\\\n  • Email delivery: Supabase built-in SMTP (free) for sign-up verification\\\\n\\\\nUSER FLOWS\\\\n 1. Resident self-sign-up → status =pending\\\\n 2. Board member logs in → Dashboard → Approves user → status =approved; role=residential or board\\\\n 3. Approved residents gain access to protected pages (Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events)\\\\n 4. Board can publish News posts & edit informational pages via point-and-click editor inside Dashboard\\\\n\\\\nDATA MODEL (SQL snippets run via Supabase SQL editor)\\\\n```\\\\ncreate table profiles (\\\\n  id uuid primary key references auth.users on delete cascade,\\\\n  email text unique,\\\\n  role text check (role in ('resident','board')) default 'resident',\\\\n  status text check (status in ('pending','approved')) default 'pending',\\\\n  created_at timestamp with time zone default now()\\\\n);\\\\n\\\\ncreate table pages (\\\\n  slug text primary key,\\\\n  title text,\\\\n  content html,\\\\n  updated_at timestamp with time zone default now()\\\\n);\\\\n\\\\ncreate table news (\\\\n  id bigserial primary key,\\\\n  title text,\\\\n  content html,\\\\n  author uuid references profiles(id),\\\\n  created_at timestamp with time zone default now()\\\\n);\\\\n\\\\ncreate table documents (\\\\n  id bigserial primary key,\\\\n  title text,\\\\n  category text check (category in ('dues','annual_meetings')),\\\\n  file_url text,\\\\n  uploaded_by uuid references profiles(id),\\\\n  created_at timestamp with time zone default now()\\\\n);\\\\n```\\\\nRLS POLICIES (samples)\\\\n```\\\\n-- Enable row level security\\\\nalter table profiles enable row level security;\\\\ncreate policy \\\\\\\"Users view own profile\\\\\\\" on profiles\\\\n  for select using (auth.uid() = id);\\\\ncreate policy \\\\\\\"Board can view all\\\\\\\" on profiles\\\\n  for select using (exists (select 1 from profiles p where p.id = auth.uid() and p.role='board'));\\\\n-- Similar policies for update/insert on other tables.\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nSTEP-BY-STEP EXECUTION\\\\n1. Local Setup\\\\n   a) Install tooling: `npm i -g vercel supabase@latest`\\\\n   b) `npx create-next-app@latest hoa-site --typescript --tailwind`\\\\n   c) `cd hoa-site && npm install @supabase/supabase-js @tiptap/react @tiptap/starter-kit`\\\\n\\\\n2. Supabase Project\\\\n   a) Owner creates Supabase project in dashboard → obtain SUPABASE_URL & SUPABASE_ANON_KEY.\\\\n   b) Run SQL blocks above (SQL editor).\\\\n   c) Configure Auth → Email provider → enable Confirm via email.\\\\n   d) Storage: create bucket `restricted-docs` (private).\\\\n\\\\n3. Environment Variables (both locally and in Vercel)\\\\n   SUPABASE_URL= <project-url>\\\\n   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY= <anon-key>\\\\n\\\\n4. Next.js Implementation\\\\n   • `/lib/supabaseClient.ts` – singleton init.\\\\n   • AuthContext provider to track user & claims (status / role from `profiles` table).\\\\n   • `withAuth(allowed)` HOC to guard pages; show pending approval notice if status!='approved'.\\\\n   • Pages & Routes\\\\n      - `/` Home (seasonal theme auto by month; CSS vars set in `ThemeProvider`).\\\\n      - `/contact`, `/bylaws`, `/schools` – public pages, editable via dashboard.\\\\n      - `/login` & `/signup` forms.\\\\n      - `/dashboard` (board only) → Tabs: Pending Approvals, Manage Pages, News, Documents.\\\\n      - `/dues`, `/annual-meetings`, `/news-events` – resident-only (approved).\\\\n   • TipTap editor component reused in Dashboard for rich-text.\\\\n\\\\n5. Board Dashboard Features\\\\n   a) Pending Approvals – table of profiles where status='pending'; Approve button → update status to 'approved'.\\\\n   b) Pages – list pages; Edit opens TipTap; Save → upsert to `pages` table.\\\\n   c) News – CRUD posts.\\\\n   d) Documents – upload to Supabase Storage bucket, create row in `documents` table.\\\\n\\\\n6. Deployment\\\\n   a) Push repo to GitHub.\\\\n   b) Connect to Vercel → Import project → set env vars.\\\\n   c) Add custom domain dunbaroakshoa.com in Vercel UI; update DNS A/CNAME records at registrar.\\\\n   d) Verify HTTPS works.\\\\n\\\\n7. Validation Checklist\\\\n   [ ] Public pages load.\\\\n   [ ] Signup email received; user in Pending list.\\\\n   [ ] Board approves user; resident can access protected pages.\\\\n   [ ] News post appears.\\\\n   [ ] Seasonal colors change (modify system date in dev to test).\\\\n\\\\n8. Documentation for HOA Board (docs/README-board.md)\\\\n   • How to log in, approve users, edit pages, post news, upload docs.\\\\n\\\\n9. Rollback / Cleanup\\\\n   • Vercel: previous deploys kept automatically – can roll back with one click.\\\\n   • Supabase: daily backups (paid) or manual export; alternatively snapshot before major changes.\\\\n   • Teardown script (if needed): `vercel rm hoa-site --yes` and delete Supabase project.\\\\n\\\\nPLACEHOLDERS TO FILL DURING EXECUTION\\\\n  <project-url> – Supabase project URL\\\\n  <anon-key>    – Supabase anon key\\\\n  DNS records   – Provided by Vercel after domain link\\\\n\\\\nEND DEP\\\"\\n}\\n###phase1###\"}]},\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":3749,\"outputTokens\":2711,\"totalTokens\":6460},\"custom\":{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-Bx0BIBIq6xXYRFhS4kV02nc2z9WMA\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1753401748,\"model\":\"o3-2025-04-16\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"###phase1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: PHASE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"All project requirements are clarified. A complete, deterministic execution plan has been designed that meets budget (<$20 /mo), provides easy content management, secure resident-only access, and seasonal theming. We are re